      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The vagus nerve is indeed a key player in box breathing's effects on the body. When we practice box breathing, our vagus nerve responds to the changed breathing pattern by activating the PNS. Specifically, the vagus nerve stimulates the release of neurotransmitters such as GABA and dopamine, which promote feelings of relaxation and calmness. Activation of the vagus nerve can also lower cortisol levels and regulate heart rate, contributing to the overall relaxing effect of box breathing.",
